# Make chargen.keys' orc barbarian, acquire one book in wizard mode, stow it,
# and dump the inventory listing so the book's SECTION HEADING can be read.
# bd inc-twr9.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/book-inventory-section.keys 1
#
# WHAT THE DUMP SHOWS. Player::InventoryManager (src/Managers.cpp:610) lists
# the contents of the current container -- the pack -- grouped by itemGroups[]
# (src/Managers.cpp:444), and it prints each group's heading from the same
# table with Lookup(ITypeNames, ...) (src/Managers.cpp:557). A book is a
# T_BOOK. Before the fix itemGroups[] had no T_BOOK entry, so a book fell
# through to sortOrder()'s 50, landed in the trailing T_ITEM group, and its
# heading read "Other Items" (src/Managers.cpp:553). After the fix it gets its
# own group and its heading reads "Books" (src/Tables.cpp:1031).
#
#   w y                      enter wizard mode and open its menu
#   Item Acquisition         the acquisition browser
#   RIGHT*7                  walk the glyph row to the book category. ItemGlyphs
#                            (src/Tables.cpp:320) puts GLYPH_BOOK,T_BOOK 7 steps
#                            along (potion 0, scroll 1, rod 2, staff 3, wand 4,
#                            eyes 5, food 6, book 7), and the header line names
#                            the category, so a miscount shows up in a dump as
#                            some other word after "Acquisition -- [...]:".
#   @until "Spellbook" DOWN  the candidate list has no menu letters and no '>'
#                            marker, so neither @choose nor @cursorto can reach
#                            a row -- walking the cursor with DOWN is the only
#                            way in. The window shows three rows and highlights
#                            the middle one, so @until stops on the pass where
#                            a spellbook name first appears at the BOTTOM of
#                            that window, and one further DOWN moves the
#                            highlight onto it. The capital S is the game's:
#                            the candidate rows print the item's name, and
#                            every T_BOOK in lib/sp_books.irh is "Spellbook
#                            [...]" (lib/m_items.irh's Tomes are T_TOME, a
#                            different type the book glyph does not reach).
#   @expect "Spellbook"      nail the name to the row before taking it.
#   ENTER                    take it. A non-stacking item lands in the In-the-
#                            Air slot and opens the inventory manager.
#   @dump:book-in-air        proves a spellbook was acquired: the In-the-Air
#                            line names it. It is drawn on the slot line, above
#                            the listing, and carries no heading.
#   s                        stow it in the backpack (src/Managers.cpp:873), so
#                            it joins the pack listing that carries the group
#                            headings.
#   @until "spellbook" PGDN  scroll the listing down until the book's own row
#                            is on screen, so the heading above it is captured
#                            too. @expect makes a scroll that ran out of list
#                            fail instead of accepting the last screen.
#   @dump:book-in-inventory  the measurement: the listing with the book in it.
#   ESC                      leave the inventory.
#   @quit                    save and quit, so the run ends cleanly.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*7
@until "Spellbook" DOWN
@expect "Spellbook"
DOWN
ENTER
@dump:book-in-air
s
@until "spellbook" PGDN
@expect "spellbook"
@dump:book-in-inventory
ESC
@quit
